hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1411","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abdul Rahman told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He did not raise his hands in any of his supplications except for rain.” Shu'bah said: I said to Thabit: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to God. I said, I heard it from Anas. He said: Glory be to God. Abu Bakr said: And in the news of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and he raised his hands, I dictated it before."
